generated_answer:
According to Local Rule 5003-1, the clerk may sign their name and enter the following without further directive from the court:

(1) an order entering default for failure to plead or otherwise defend under Fed. R. Bankr. P. 7055;
(2) a subpoena for a party not represented by an attorney;
(3) an order of discharge;
(4) an order of dismissal, as directed by Local Rules 2003-1(a), 2082-1(b), 2083-1(e) and 7041-1, or similar dismissal orders arising from the failure of the debtor to respond to a motion to dismiss; and
(5) any other order or document that does not require approval or order by the court under Fed. R. Civ. P. 77(c).
